<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.01.320       Potentially
dangerous animal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.01.330       Premises.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.01.340       Proper
enclosure.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.01.350       Provocation
or provoke.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.01.360       Service
or assistive animal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.01.370       Severe
injury.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.01.380       Under
control.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.01.390       Vicious.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.01.400       Warning
sign.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><a name="_Hlk140133035"></a><a name="_Hlk140132900"><b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.010 
Application of chapter.</span></b></a><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The definitions in this chapter apply throughout this
title unless the context clearly requires otherwise.</span><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 19638 § 2,
2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.020 
Abate.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Abate&quot; means to terminate or remedy any violation by
reasonable and lawful means determined by the manager.  (Ord. 19638 § 3, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.030 
Adequate care.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Adequate care&quot; means providing to an animal:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
Species-appropriate food or feed and water that is easily accessible to the
animal and of sufficient quantity and quality to sustain the animal in good
health;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
A structure that:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Is sufficient to protect the animal from wind, rain, snow, cold, heat, or
sun;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Has bedding to permit the animal to remain dry, reasonably clean, and free
of excess feces and to maintain a normal body temperature, and that allows the
animal to turn around freely, sit, stand, and lie without restriction; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  Does not injure, disfigure or physically impair the animal; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
Adequate veterinary medical care.  (Ord. 19638 § 4, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.040 
Altered.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Altered&quot; means spayed or neutered.  (Ord. 19638 § 5, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.050 
Animal.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Animal&quot; means any living amphibian, bird, fish, reptile or
mammal, except a human.  (Ord. 19638 § 6, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.060 
Animal care and control authority.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Animal care and control authority&quot; means the
regional animal services section of the records and licensing services
division, acting alone or in concert with other municipalities, to enforce
animal care and control laws and for the shelter and welfare of animals.  (Ord.
19638 § 7, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.070 
Animal care and control officer.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Animal care and control officer&quot; means any
individual employed, contracted, or appointed by the animal care and control
authority to aide in enforcing this title or any other law or ordinance
relating to the care and licensing of animals, control of animals, or seizure
and impoundment of animals.  &quot;Animal care and control officer&quot;
includes any state or municipal peace officer, sheriff, or other employee whose
duties in whole or in part include assignments that involve the seizure and
taking into custody of any animal.  (Ord. 19638 § 8, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.080 
Animal shelter.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Animal shelter&quot; means a facility used to
house or contain stray, homeless, abandoned, or unwanted animals, and that is
owned, operated, or maintained by a public body, an established humane society,
animal welfare society, society for the prevention of cruelty to animals, or
other nonprofit organization or person devoted to the welfare, protection, and
humane treatment of animals.  (Ord. 19638 § 9, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.090 
At large.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;At large&quot; means any animal off the premises of its owner
and not under control of a competent person.  (Ord. 19638 § 10, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.100 
Companion animal.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Companion animal&quot; means any species of
animal commonly kept for companionship, including working dogs and excluding
exotic animals.  (Ord. 19638 § 11, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.110 
Competent person.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Competent person&quot; means a person able to
sufficiently care for, control, and restrain a particular animal, and who has
the capacity to exercise sound judgment regarding the rights and safety of
others.  (Ord. 19638 § 12, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.120 
Dangerous animal.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'>            <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>A.  &quot;Dangerous animal&quot; means any animal that:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Inflicts severe injury on or causes the death of a human being without
provocation;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Inflicts severe injury on or causes the death of a domesticated animal
without provocation;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  Has been previously found to be potentially dangerous or vicious because of
injury inflicted on a human, the owner having received notice of such, and the
animal again bites, attacks, or endangers the safety of humans;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.  Enters onto private property without the consent of the owner or occupant
and, regardless of provocation, engages in conduct meeting subsection A.1.,
A.2., or A.3. of this section; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
5.  Jointly engages, with one or more animals, in conduct meeting A.1., A.2.,
A.3., or A.4. of this section, in which case all animals may be deemed
dangerous, absent an affirmative demonstration that a specific animal was not
responsible for a qualifying act.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
An animal shall not be declared a &quot;dangerous animal&quot; if:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  The threat, injury, or bite alleged to have been committed by the animal
was sustained by a person who was at the time committing a willful trespass
upon the premises occupied by the owner of the animal, or who was abusing or
assaulting the animal, or who was committing or attempting to commit a crime. 
This exclusion does not apply to actions taken in defense of oneself, other
humans, animals, or property; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  The animal has not been previously found to be potentially dangerous,
vicious, or dangerous, and the severe injury or death is to a domesticated
animal other than pets or large livestock.  (Ord. 19638 § 13, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.130 
Director.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Director&quot; means the director of public health - Seattle
&amp; King County or designee.  However, for the purposes of K.C.C. chapter
11.02, &quot;director&quot; means the director of the department of executive
services or designee.  (Ord. 19638 § 14, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.140 
Domesticated animal.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Domesticated animal&quot; means any animal that
is a companion animal, a service or assistive animal, livestock, or poultry. 
(Ord. 19638 § 15, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.150 
Euthanasia.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Euthanasia&quot; means the humane destruction of an animal,
accomplished by a method that involves near instantaneous unconsciousness and
immediate death or by a method that causes painless loss of consciousness and
death during the loss of consciousness.  (Ord. 19638 § 16, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.160 
Exotic animal.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Exotic animal&quot; means any of the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
Species of snakes capable of inflicting serious physical harm or death to human
beings;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
Nonhuman primates and prosimians;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
Bears;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D. 
Nondomesticated species of felines;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E. 
Nondomesticated species of canines and their hybrids, including wolf and coyote
hybrids; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F. 
Any species within the order Crocodylia, including but not limited to
alligators, crocodiles, caimans, and gavials.  (Ord. 19638 § 17, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.170 
Feral.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Feral&quot; means any animal belonging to a species typically
domesticated that lives and behaves like a wild animal.  (Ord. 19638 § 18, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.180 
Grooming service.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Grooming service&quot; means any public or
private place or establishment where animals are bathed, clipped, or combed to
enhance either their aesthetic value or health, or both, for a fee.  (Ord. 19638
§ 19, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.190 
Harbor, keep, or maintain.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Harbor, keep, or maintain&quot; means:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
Providing animal care, shelter, protection, refuge, food, or nourishment; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
Having custody of an animal.  (Ord. 19638 § 20, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.200 
Hobby cattery.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  &quot;Hobby cattery&quot; means a noncommercial cattery
at or adjoining a private residence where four or more nonjuvenile cats are
bred or kept for exhibition or for enjoyment.  (Ord. 19638 § 21, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.210 
Hobby kennel.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Hobby kennel&quot; means a noncommercial kennel at or adjoining
a private residence where four or more nonjuvenile dogs are bred or kept for
any combination of hunting, training, exhibition, field or obedience trials,
working, or enjoyment.  (Ord. 19638 § 22, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.220 
Juvenile.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Juvenile&quot; means any dog or cat under six months old.  (Ord.
19638 § 23, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.230 
King County.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;King County&quot; means the unincorporated area of King County,
Washington, and any jurisdiction that has an interlocal agreement with King
County for regional animal services.  (Ord. 19638 § 24, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.240 
Livestock.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Livestock&quot; has the same meaning as in RCW 16.57.010.  (Ord.
19638 § 25, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.250 
Mammal.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Mammal&quot; means any animal of a class of warm-blooded
vertebrate animals that nourish their young with milk secreted by mammary
glands and have skin generally covered with hair, and includes bats.  (Ord. 19638
§ 26, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.260 
Manager.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Manager&quot; means the manager of the regional animal services
section of the records and licensing services division, or the manager's
designees.  (Ord. 19638 § 27, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.270 
Muzzle.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Muzzle&quot; means a device that prevents an animal from biting
others and does not cause injury to the animal nor inhibit its vision,
respiration, or panting.  (Ord. 19638 § 28, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.280 
Owner.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Owner&quot; means any person who harbors, keeps, maintains, or
has control of an animal except for individuals or organizations involved with
providing care to a feral cat colony, such as trap, neuter, and release
programs.  (Ord. 19638 § 29, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.290 
Pack.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Pack&quot; means any group of two or more animals running at
large.  (Ord. 19638 § 30, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.300 
Person.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  &quot;Person&quot; means any individual, partnership, firm, company,
corporation, association, or other legal entity.  (Ord. 19638 § 31, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.310 
Pet.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
&quot;Pet&quot; means any dog or any nonferal cat.  (Ord. 19638 § 32, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.320 
Potentially dangerous animal.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
&quot;Potentially dangerous animal&quot; means any animal that when unprovoked:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Bites or inflicts injury on a human or domesticated animal;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Chases or approaches a person upon the streets, sidewalks, or any public
grounds in a menacing fashion or apparent attitude of attack;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  Has a known propensity, tendency, or disposition to attack, to cause
injury,</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>or
otherwise to threaten the safety of humans or domestic animals; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.  Jointly engages, with one or more animals in conduct meeting subsections
A.1., A.2., or A.3., of this section, in which case all animals are deemed
potentially dangerous, absent an affirmative demonstration that a specific
animal was not responsible for a qualifying act.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
Regardless of provocation, an animal is a &quot;potentially dangerous
animal&quot; if it enters onto private property without the consent of the
owner or occupant and bites a human or animal or chases or approaches a person
in a menacing fashion or apparent attitude of attack.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
An animal shall not be declared a &quot;potentially dangerous animal&quot; if
the threat, injury, or bite alleged to have been committed by the animal was
sustained by a person who was at the time committing a willful trespass upon
the premises occupied by the owner of the animal, or who was abusing or
assaulting the animal, or who was committing, or attempting to commit a crime.
This exclusion does not apply to actions taken in defense of oneself, other
humans, animals, or property.  (Ord. 19638 § 33, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.330 
Premises.</span></b>  <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>&quot;Premises&quot; means the real property or enclosed space that an
animal's owner has a legal or equitable right to occupy, including a dwelling
unit.  &quot;Premises&quot; does not extend into areas of common ownership or
use, such as an apartment lobby or public transportation.  (Ord. 19638 § 34, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.340 
Proper enclosure.</span></b>  <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&quot;Proper enclosure&quot; means, while on its owner's
premises, an animal is securely confined indoors or in an enclosed and locked
pen or structure, suitable to prevent the entry of young children and designed
to prevent the animal from escaping.  The pen or structure must fully enclose
the animal, consist of secure sides, top, and bottom, and provide protection
from the elements.  (Ord. 19638 § 35, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.350 
Provocation or provoke.</span></b>  <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&quot;Provocation&quot; or &quot;provoke&quot; means to
torment, agitate, or harass an animal immediately before the attack, chase, or
menacing behavior.  &quot;Provocation&quot; or &quot;provoke&quot; does not
include actions taken to defend oneself, other humans, animals, or property. 
(Ord. 19638 § 36, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.360 
Service or assistive animal.</span></b>  <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&quot;Service or assistive animal&quot; has the same
meaning as in K.C.C. 12.22.020*.  (Ord. 19638 § 37, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's
note:  K.C.C. 12.22.020 was amended by Ordinance 19977, Section 27, which
removed the definition of &quot;service or assistive animal&quot; from the
section.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.370 
Severe injury.</span></b>  <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&quot;Severe injury&quot; means any physical injury that
results in:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
One or more broken bones;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
One or more disfiguring lacerations, avulsions, cuts or puncture wounds
requiring medical attention, including, but not limited to, one or more
sutures, steri strips or staples;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
Permanent nerve damage; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D. 
Transmittal of an infectious or contagious disease.  (Ord. 19638 § 38, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.380 
Under control.</span></b>  <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&quot;Under control&quot; means a domesticated animal is
restrained, by a human using a leash or competent and effective voice or signal
control, from approaching any bystander or other domesticated animal and from
causing property damage.  (Ord. 19638 § 39, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.390 
Vicious.</span></b>  <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>&quot;Vicious&quot; means having performed the act of, or having the
propensity to do any act, endangering the safety of any human, animal, or
property of another, including, but not limited to, biting a human being, or
attacking a human being or domesticated animal without provocation.  (Ord. 19638
§ 40, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.01.400 
Warning sign.</span></b>  <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&quot;Warning sign&quot; means a conspicuously displayed
sign containing clearly visible words, along with a symbol informing those who
are incapable of reading, warning of a potentially dangerous or dangerous
animal on the property.  (Ord. 19638 § 41, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc320003735"></a><a name="_Toc320003759"></a><a
name="_Toc444847780">11.02   REGIONAL ANIMAL SERVICES SECTION</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b>Sections:</b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.02.010       Established.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.02.020       Manager
- established - compensation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.02.030       Agreements
- authorization.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.02.040       Agreements
- concessions - revenue for regional animal services.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.02.050       Agreements
- advertising, sponsorship, naming rights - for regional animal services programs
- restrictions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.02.060       Gifts,
bequests, and donations - solicitation and acceptance - deposit in animal
bequest fund - restrictions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:0in;
margin-left:99.0pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-99.0pt;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>         11.02.070       Rules
- adoption and enforcement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.02.010 
Established.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  A regional animal services section is established in the records and
licensing services division.  This chapter designates the regional animal
services section as the agency authorized to provide animal care services and enforce
animal control laws.  (<a name="_Hlk140150090">Ord. 19638 § 42, 2023:  </a>Ord.
16861 § 7, 2010:  Ord. 15971 § 57, 2007:  Ord. 15801 § 1, 2007:  Ord. 14498 <a
name="OLE_LINK1">§ </a>6, 2002:  Ord. 1361 § 4, 1972:  Ord. 1269 § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.02.020 
Manager - established - compensation</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.  Within the regional animal services section, the
position of manager is established, to be compensated at a rate in accordance
with county personnel policies.  (Ord. 19638 § 43, 2023:  Ord. 16861 § 8,
2010:  Ord. 15801 § 2, 2007:  Ord. 14498 § 7, 2002: Ord. 6370 § 1, 1983:  Ord.
1269 § 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.02.030 
Agreements - authorization.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The county executive is authorized to enter into
agreements with public agencies as defined in chapter 39.34 RCW for animal
licensing and enforcement of animal care and control ordinances, and with other
legal entities for the purpose of disposing of animal remains.  (Ord. 19638 § 44,
2023:  Ord. 15801 § 3, 2007:  Ord. 6370 § 2, 1983:  Ord. 1370 § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            <b>11.02.040  Agreements
- concessions - revenue for regional animal services.</b>  The director of the
department of executive services is authorized to enter into concession
agreements with vendors to sell animal-related products and services at the
King County animal shelter and at other county facilities and events.  The
revenue from these concession agreements shall be applied solely to regional
animal services.  (Ord. 16861 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span> 9,
2010).</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>&nbsp;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'><b>            11.02.050  Agreements
- advertising, sponsorship, naming rights - for regional animal services
programs - restrictions.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            A.  The director may
negotiate and enter into advertising, sponsorship, and naming rights agreements
to provide financial support for regional animal services programs. 
Advertising is restricted to commercial speech.</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            B.  Advertisers and
sponsors shall abide by the nondiscrimination requirements of Section 840 of
the King County Charter and K.C.C. Title 12.  Furthermore, an advertising,
sponsorship or naming rights agreement may not result in advertisement of
spirits or tobacco products in accordance with K.C.C. chapter 12.51.</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            C.  The director may
impose additional subject-matter restrictions on advertising, sponsorship and
naming rights agreements consistent with applicable law.</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            D.  Revenue generated
from advertising, sponsorships and naming rights agreements entered into under
this section must be applied solely to regional animal services.  (Ord. 19638 §
45, 2023:  Ord. 16861 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span> 11, 2010).</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>&nbsp;</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            <b>11.02.060  Gifts,
bequests, and donations - solicitation and acceptance - deposit in animal
bequest fund - restrictions.</b></p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            A.  Consistent with
K.C.C. chapter 3.04, the executive, the director, the manager of the records
and licensing services division, the manager, the council and councilmembers
and staff who report directly to those officers or officials and who do so at
those officers' or officials' direction, may solicit and accept from the
general public and business communities and all other persons, gifts, bequests,
and donations to the county in support of regional animal services.</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            B.  All gifts, bequests
and donations of money to the county for regional animal services must be
deposited and credited to the animal bequest fund created under K.C.C. 4A.200.130.</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>            C.  The director shall
assure that expenditures from gifts, bequests, or donations are consistent with
the terms, if any, requested by their grantors.  (Ord. 19638 § 46, 2023:  Ord.
16861 § 10, 2010).</p>

<p class=Normal style='text-align:justify'>&nbsp;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.02.070 
Rules - adoption and enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The manager may adopt and enforce rules under the
procedures specified in K.C.C. chapter 2.98 that are consistent with this
title.  (Ord. 19638 § 47, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

