<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>(Ord. 19638 <span style='letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>§</span> 52, 2023:  Ord. 16861 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span>
16, 2010:  Ord. 16309 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span> 3, 2008:  <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 15801 § 8, 2007: </span> Ord. 14790 <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§ </span>2, 2003:  Ord. 14521 § 2, 2002:  Ord.
14498 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§ </span>9, 2002:  Ord. 13335 § 2,
1998:  Ord. 12921 § 1, 1997:  Ord. 12542 § 1, 1996:  Ord. 11404 § 3, 1994: 
Ord. 10809 § 6, 1993:  Ord. 10423 § 5, 1992:  Ord. 10168 § 2, 1991:  Ord. 7861
§ 1, 1986:  Ord. 7416 § 2, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            <b>11.04.060  Hobby
kennel or hobby cattery licenses - required - limitations - requirements -
issuance and maintenance.</b></span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            A.  It is a violation of
this chapter for any person to operate a hobby kennel or hobby cattery unless
the person possesses and complies with a hobby kennel or hobby cattery license.</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            B.  Each animal maintained
at a hobby kennel or hobby cattery must be licensed individually under K.C.C.
11.04.030.</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            C.  Any hobby kennel or
hobby cattery license shall limit the total number of pets based on:</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>              1.  Animal age and size;</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>              2.  Breed characteristics;
in particular, in the case of dogs, the pitch and volume of their barks;</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>              3.  The amount of lot area,
though the maximum number may not exceed:</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>                a.  three on lots of
less than twenty thousand square feet;</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>                b.  five on lots between
twenty thousand and thirty-five thousand square feet, except that a maximum of
three total pets may remain unaltered; and</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>                c.  an additional two
pets for each acre of lot area beyond thirty-five thousand square feet, up to a
maximum of twenty, except that a maximum of three total pets may remain
unaltered;</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>              4.  The layout and size of
any structure for sheltering the pets; and</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>              5.  The zoning
classification where the hobby kennel or hobby cattery would be maintained.</span></p>

<p class=tx style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            D.  Hobby kennels and hobby
catteries shall comply with the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>              1.  All open
run areas must be completely surrounded by a six-foot fence set back at least
twenty feet from all property lines, though this requirement may be modified
for hobby catteries, as long as the open run area contains the cats and
prohibits the entrance of children.  For purposes of this section, &quot;open
run area&quot; means that area where the pets are sheltered or maintained.  If
there is no area set aside for sheltering or maintaining the pets within the
property lines of the <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>premises, the twenty-foot
setback does not apply.  The property lines of premises not containing an open
run area must be completely surrounded by a six-foot fence;</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Commercial signs or other appearances advertising the hobby kennel or hobby
cattery are not permitted on the premises, except for those advertising the
sale of the allowable offspring, as set forth in this section;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  The manager may require setbacks, fencing, screening, or soundproofing, as
necessary to ensure compatibility of the hobby kennel or hobby cattery with the
surrounding neighborhood.  Factors to be considered in determining compatibility
are:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
a.  statements of surrounding neighbors relative to maintenance of a hobby
kennel or hobby cattery at the address applied for;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
b.  history of verified animal care and control complaints relating to the
applicant’s pets;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
c.  facility specifications or dimensions in which the pets are to be
maintained;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
d.  animal size, type and characteristics of breed; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
e.  the zoning classification of the premises on which the hobby kennel or
hobby cattery is maintained;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.  The hobby kennel or hobby cattery shall limit pet reproduction to no more
than one litter per license year per female dog and two litters per license
year per female cat; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
5.  Each pet in the hobby kennel or hobby cattery must have the following
current immunizations:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
a.  for dogs over three months old, distemper, hepatitis, parainfluenza and
parvo virus (DA2PP) inoculation ;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
b.  for cats over two months old, feline herpesvirus 1, calicivirus, and
panleukopenia virus (FVRCP) inoculation; and </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
c.  for all pets over four months old, rabies inoculation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E. 
A hobby kennel or hobby cattery license remains valid for one year, subject to
renewal, and  may be terminated if the facility fails to comply with this
section.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F. 
For applicants who cannot meet the requirements of this section, the manager
may issue a hobby kennel or hobby cattery license authorizing persons to retain
more than three pets if:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  The applicant keeps the pets for enjoyment only, and not as a commercial
enterprise;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  The applicant keeps only those pets in the applicant's possession at the
time of license issuance.  The license must identify each pet and allow
possession of more animals than would otherwise be allowed only until the death
or relocation of those specific animals;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  The licensed facility provides a living environment with sufficient area,
dimension, design, ventilation, and cleanliness to assure the comfort and lack
of distress of each animal and is operated and maintained in a manner that is
compatible with neighboring properties; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.  The pets have no additional litters until the total number of pets is
reduced to three or fewer.  (  Ord. 19638 § 54, 2023:  Ord. 16861 § 18, 2010:  Ord.
15801 § 10, 2007:  Ord. 11792 § 5, 1995:  Ord. 10423 § 11, 1992:  Ord. 10168 §
4, 1991:  Ord. 6370 § 5, 1983:  Ord. 4610 § 3, 1979: Ord. 4269 § 1, 1979:  Ord.
2428 § 3, 1975:  Ord. 1396 Art. II § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.070 
Animal shelters, hobby kennels, hobby catteries, or pet shops - reporting
required.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  Each animal shelter, hobby kennel, hobby cattery or pet shop shall monthly
provide the manager with a list of all pets that it has given away or sold. 
The list must include the origin, age, sex, color, breed, altered status and,
if applicable, microchip number and license number of each pet given away or
sold and the new owner's name, address and, if available, email address and
telephone number.  (Ord. 19638 § 55, 2023:  Ord. 16861 § 19, 2010:  Ord. 15801
§ 11, 2007:  Ord. 10423 § 7, 1992:  Ord. 2428 § 4, 1975:  Ord. 1396 Art. II §
5, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.150 
Licenses, registration, permits - hobby kennel or hobby cattery - revocation,
suspension, or refusal to renew.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to imposing penalties provided in this
title, the manager may condition, revoke, suspend, or refuse to renew any hobby
kennel</span> <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>license
or hobby cattery</span> <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>license for failure to comply with any condition of the license or
permit or for any violation of this title.  Enforcement is stayed during the
pendency of an appeal filed in accordance with K.C.C. 11.04.260.  (Ord. 19638 §
57, 2010:  Ord. 16861 § 22, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 14, 2007:  Ord. 3232 § 11,
1977:  Ord. 2428 § 10, 1975:  Ord. 1396 Art. II § 13, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.160 
Licenses, registration, permits - hobby kennel or hobby cattery - revocation or
refusal waiting period.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  An applicant who has had a license permit, or
registration revoked or a renewal refused shall not be issued a hobby kennel
license or a hobby cattery license for one year after the revocation or refusal
to renew becomes final.  (Ord. 19638 § 58, 2023:  Ord. 16861 § 23, 2010:  Ord.
15801 § 15, 2007:  Ord. 3232 § 12, 1977:  Ord. 1396 Art. II § 14, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser’s
note:  Language added but not underlined in Ordinance 16861.  See K.C.C.
1.24.075.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal align=center style='text-align:center'><b>III.  ENFORCEMENT,
PENALTIES AND PROCEDURES</b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.170 
Enforcement powers.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
The manager is authorized to take such lawful action as appropriate to enforce:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  This title;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Ordinance 10870, as amended, and K.C.C. Title 21A</span> <span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>pertaining to
animals; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  The laws of Washington pertaining to animals.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
The manager, while pursuing or observing any animal in violation of this title,
may enter upon any public or private property, except any building designated
for and used for private purposes, for the purpose of abating the animal
violation being pursued or observed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
The manager may inspect any facilities licensed or permitted under this title
to ensure compliance with this title and the applicable permit or license.  (Ord.
19638 § 60, 2023:  Ord. 16861 § 26, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 18, 2007:  Ord. 14498 §
11, 2002:  Ord. 11792 § 8, 1995:  Ord. 3980 § 3, 1978:  Ord. 2771 § 2, 1976: 
Ord. 2428 § 11, 1975:  Ord. 1396 Art. III § 1, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.174 
Assistance with enforcement and carrying out BOH chapter 8.04, Rabies.</b>  The
manager is authorized to assist the director in enforcing and carrying out BOH
chapter 8.04 of the King County Board of Health Code.</span>  <span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord. 19638 § 91,
2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.180 
Violations - deemed public nuisances - abatement.</span></b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  All violations of
this title are detrimental to public health, safety and welfare and are deemed
public nuisances, subject to abatement and other enforcement in accordance with
this title or as otherwise authorized by law or equity.  (Ord. 19638 § 61, 2023: 
Ord. 16861 § 27, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 19, 2007:  Ord. 1396 Art. III § 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.200 
Violations - civil penalty.</b>  In addition to or as an alternative to any
other penalty provided in this title  or by law, any person whose animal is
maintained in violation of this title shall incur a civil penalty as specified
by K.C.C. 11.04.035.  All civil penalties assessed will be assessed and
collected in accordance with the procedure specified in this title.  (Ord. 19638
§ 63, 2023:  Ord. 15801 § 20, 2007:  Ord. 10168 § 6, 1991:  Ord. 7923 § 2,
1987:  Ord. 6370 § 6, 1983:  Ord. 4610 § 5, 1979:  Ord. 3548 § 6, 1978:  Ord.
1396 Art. III § 4, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.210 
Apprehending and impounding - retention - redemption.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
The manager may apprehend and impound any animal found to be at large.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
The manager shall make reasonable efforts to serve the owner with written
notice specifying the basis for impoundment and the requirements for regaining
custody of the animal, if applicable.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
Animals impounded under this section must be retained as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Any currently licensed animal must be held for five calendar days after
telephone contact to the owner or posting notice of impoundment on the front
door of the living unit of the owner, or for at least fourteen calendar days
after sending the owner notice of impoundment by regular mail;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Any animal whose owner cannot be determined by license or other means must
be held for at least three calendar days from the time of impoundment, unless
otherwise provided by law;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  The manager may provide medical care to an animal during impoundment.  Any
animal suffering from serious injury or disease may be euthanized; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.  Feral cats that are altered and ear tipped are exempt from the holding
periods in this subsection and are subject to immediate disposition, at the
discretion of the manager, which may include returning the feral cat to the
location where it was found.</span> <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>        </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Times New Roman",serif'>            </span><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>D.  Except where
return of the animal is restricted by law, order of the manager, order of the
hearing examiner, or order of a court, an owner may redeem the animal by paying
the redemption and kenneling fees provided in K.C.C. 11.04.035 and any expenses
the manager incurred altering, microchipping, and providing necessary medical
care to the animal during the animal's period of impoundment.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E. 
Any animal not redeemed within the time required by subsection C. of this
section may be:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Made available for adoption at the fee provided in K.C.C. 11.04.035;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Transferred to another animal welfare organization for adoption;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  Placed into foster care;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.  Sold at public auction; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
5.  Euthanized.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F. 
The county shall not sell any animals for the purposes of medical research to
any research institute or any other purchasers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G. 
All pets adopted from the King County animal shelter must be altered and
microchipped before adoption.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H. 
Any pet impounded more than once shall be microchipped before redemption</span><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>.  (Ord. 19638 <span style='letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>§</span> 64, 2023:  Ord. 16861 <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span>
28, 2010:  <span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 15801 § 21, 2007: </span> Ord.
11920 § 1, 1995:  Ord. 10423 § 23, 1992:  Ord. 10168 § 7, 1991:  Ord. 7986 § 2,
1987:  Ord. 7871, 1986:  Ord. 6370 § 7, 1983:  Ord. 6243 § 1, 1982:  Ord. 6049,
1982:  Ord. 5805 § 3, 1981: Ord. 2428 § 12, 1975:  Ord. 1396 Art. III § 5,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.220 
Additional enforcement.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  Notwithstanding the existence or use of any other
remedy, the manager may seek legal or equitable relief to enjoin acts or
practices and abate any conditions that constitute a violation of this title. 
(Ord. 19638 § 65, 2023:  Ord. 16861 § 29, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 22, 2007:  Ord.
1396 Art. III § 6, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.222 
Removal of animal from county for repeated notices and orders of violation.</span></b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  In addition to
other remedies provided in this title, the manager may order an animal removed
from the county when the animal has been the subject of five or more notices
and orders of violation in any two-year period.</span><a name="_Hlk141100775">  </a><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord. 19638 § 66,
2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.225 
Additional enforcement - to further purposes of title - animal cruelty.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            A.  The
manager may prohibit a person who violates K.C.C. 11.04.250 from owning, caring
for, or residing with any animals for up to two years, if the manager
determines that the prohibition furthers the purposes of this title.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            B.  The
manager may prohibit a person convicted of animal cruelty from owning, caring
for, or residing with any animals, consistent with RCW 16.52.200.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            C.  The manager
may enforce this section through the notice and order process in K.C.C.
11.04.260.  The notice and order is subject to appeal, in accordance with
K.C.C. 11.04.270.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            D.  The
manager may impound an animal owned, cared for, or residing with a person
contrary to this section.  If an animal is impounded under this section, then
the procedures in RCW 16.52.085 shall apply.  (<a name="_Hlk141100788">Ord. 19638
§ 67. 2023:  </a><span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 15801 § 66, 2007).</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.230 
Public nuisances - defined and prohibited.</span></b><span style='font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The following constitute public
nuisances and are prohibited:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
Any public nuisance relating to animal care and control known at common law or
in equity jurisprudence;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
A domesticated animal that enters any area where food is stored, prepared,
served, or sold to the public; however, this subsection B.2. does not apply to
service or assistive animals;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.
 While in heat, for a pet to be accessible to males of the same species, except
for males of the same species, except for planned breeding;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D. 
A domesticated animal chases, runs after, or jumps at people riding in vehicles
, or on bicycles, skateboards, roller skates, or other wheeled devices in
public areas;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E. 
A domesticated animal that menaces a person or other domesticated animals under
circumstances not meeting the definition of &quot;potentially dangerous&quot;;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F. 
A domesticated animal that meets the definition of &quot;potentially dangerous
animal&quot; or &quot;dangerous animal.&quot;  In addition, the provisions of
this chapter relating to potentially dangerous animals or dangerous animals
shall apply;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G. 
A domesticated animal that violates any provision of this title after a final
determination of the animal being potentially dangerous, vicious, or dangerous;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H. 
Failure to comply with a manager's order related to a potentially dangerous,
vicious or dangerous animal;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I. 
A domesticated animal leaving the owner's premises and thereafter cause damage
to anything of value;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            J. 
A domesticated animal chasing livestock, unless engaged in the specific work of
herding that livestock, as approved by the livestock's owner;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            K. 
A domesticated animal making noise, to an unreasonable degree, in such a manner
as to disturb a person or neighborhood;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            L. 
A domesticated animal entering upon a person's property or premises without that
person's permission;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            M. 
Failure to obtain care for a domesticated animal from a licensed veterinarian
when the owner knows the animal has a contagious disease;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            N. 
Bringing into King County, breeding, or having custody or control, even
temporarily, of a potentially dangerous wild animal as defined in chapter 16.30
RCW as of June 17, 2023.  For purposes of this chapter, wolf hybrids and coyote
hybrids are potentially dangerous wild animals;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            O. 
For a dog to be at large, or be at large in a pack, except in designated
off-leash areas or while engaged in obedience training, lawful hunting
activity, lawful organized competition, lawful training in preparation for such
hunting or competition, herding livestock, or sanctioned search and rescue
activities;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            P. 
Failure to license a pet, as required by K.C.C. 11.04.030;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Q. 
Sell, barter, or otherwise transfer ownership of any animal without the
appropriate license or permit;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            R. 
Stake, tether, or keep any animal on public property without prior written
consent of the public entity that owns the premises;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            S. 
Fail to remove the feces of their domesticated animal from another's premises
and deposit the same in an appropriate receptacle;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            T. 
Possess an exotic animal in violation of K.C.C. 11.28.030;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            U. 
Fail to comply with an order related to an animal designated as potentially
dangerous, vicious, or dangerous;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            V. 
Fail to timely obtain or renew a potentially dangerous registration or a
dangerous animal registration;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            W. 
Bring a potentially dangerous or dangerous animal into King County without
meeting the requirements of K.C.C. 11.04.275 or 11.04.285;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            X. 
Release any animal from any confinement, vehicle, or restraint unless the
release is with the owner's permission, necessary for the animal's immediate
health and safety, or undertaken by peace, animal care, or humane officers;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Y. 
Sell, offer for sale, barter, or give away any fowl under three weeks old or
any rabbit under two months old, as a companion animal, toy, premium, or
novelty, or to color, dye, stain, or otherwise change the natural color of any
such a fowl or rabbit; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Z. 
Violate the prohibition on owning, caring for, or residing with any animals
under K.C.C. 11.04.225.  (Ord. 19638 § 68. 2023:  Ord. 18000 § 1. 2015:  Ord. 14498
§ 12, 2002:  Ord. 7923 § 3, 1987:  Ord. 6370 § 8, 1983:  Ord. 1396 Art. III §
7, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            11.04.232  Stock restricted
area.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>  All of King
County, except national forest lands owned by the federal government, is
designated a stock restricted area in which it is unlawful to permit livestock,
as defined in K.C.C. 21A.06.695, to run at large.  (Ord. 11792 § 9, 1995:  Ord.
5975 § 1, 1982<span style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.  Formerly K.C.C. 11.24.010</span>).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.234 
Harboring, keeping, or maintenance of exotic animal prohibited - exception -
impoundment.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            </span></b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>A.  A person may
not harbor, keep, or maintain an exotic animal, unless an exception in RCW
16.30.020 applies.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
An exotic animal harbored, kept or maintained in violation of this section is
subject to impoundment.  If an animal is impounded under this section, the
procedures in RCW 16.30.040(2) through (6) shall apply.  (Ord. 19638 § 96.
2023:  Ord. 15801 § 50, 2007:  Ord. 11340 § 2, 1994:  Ord. 2473 § 3, 1975.  Formerly
K.C.C. 11.28.030.).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.250 
Violations - specified acts or failures to act - impoundment.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
It is a violation of this chapter for any person to:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Injure or cause the death of any animal by any means causing it fright or
pain;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Cause or allow any animal to endure pain, suffering or injury;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>              3. <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'> Fail or neglect to aid or attempt to alleviate
pain, suffering or injury the person has caused any animal;</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          4.  Deprive any animal of care
sufficient to maintain its health and well-being, by failing to provide:</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            a.  food of sufficient
quantity or quality to allow for normal growth, body weight, health, and vigor;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            b.  sufficient potable
water, which must be always available;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            c.  containers for food and
water that allow the animal easy access;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            d.  a living environment
with sufficient area, dimension, design, ventilation, and cleanliness to assure
the animal's comfort and lack of distress;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            e.  shelter sufficient to
protect against cold or heat; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            f.  veterinary care
necessary to relieve distress from injury, neglect or disease;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          5.  Fail to provide adequate
care to any animal, even if the failure does not result in the animal actually
enduring pain, suffering or injury;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          6.  Leave or confine any
animal unattended in a motor vehicle or enclosed space if the animal could be
harmed or killed by exposure to excessive heat, cold, lack of ventilation or
lack of necessary water;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          7.  Restrain a dog outside by
a tether, except in compliance with RCW 16.52.350.  Each incident involving a
violation of this subsection G. is a separate nuisance;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>              8.  Lay out or expose any
kind of poison, or to leave exposed any poison food or drink for humans, animals
or fowl, or any deadly substance or fluid, alone or mingled</span> <span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>with any other substance or fluid, on
any premises or in any unenclosed place, or to aid or abet any person in so
doing, unless in accordance with RCW 16.52.190;</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>              9.  Torment, torture,
beat, kick, strike, or harass any dog used by a police department for police
work, or otherwise interfere with the use of any such dog for police work; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
10.  Abandon any domesticated animal, excluding feral cats.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
B.  The manager may impound an animal that has been subject to any of the acts,
or failures to act, in this section.  If an animal is impounded under this
section, then the procedures in RCW 16.52.085 shall apply.  (Ord. 19638 § 70,
2023:  Ord. 16861 § 30, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 24, 2007:  Ord. 14498 § 13, 2002:  Ord.
1396 Art. III § 8, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.260 
Violations - proceedings to abate - notice and order.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
Whenever the manager finds a violation of this title, the manager shall
commence proceedings the abate each violation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
The manager shall issue a notice of violation and an order directed to the
owner or the person presumed to be the owner of the animal maintained in
violation of this chapter.  The notice and order shall contain:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  The name and address, if known, of the violator;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  The license number, if available, and description of the animal in
violation sufficient for identification;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  A statement to the effect that the manager has found a violation of this
title, including reference to the specific sections of code or statute violated
and, where relevant, reference to the specific sections of code or statute
authorizing removal of the animal;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.a.  A statement of the action the manager may require for abating the
violation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
b.  The order may require that the abatement, if any, be completed within a
specified time from the order, as the manager determines reasonable.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
c.  If the manager has determined to assess a civil penalty, the order must
require that the penalty shall be paid within twenty-four days from the order;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
5.  Statements advising that if any required abatement is not commenced within
the time specified, the manager shall proceed to abate and charge the abatement
costs against the violator; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
6.  Statements advising:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
a.  that a person having a legal interest in the animal may appeal the notice
of violation and order or any action of the manager to the office of the
hearing examiner by filing an appeal with the manager in accordance with K.C.C.
20.22.080; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>               
b.  that failure to appeal constitutes a waiver of all rights to an
administrative hearing and a final determination of the matter.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
The notice and order must be served on the violator in one of the following
ways:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Personally;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  By mailing a copy of the notice of violation and order by certified mail,
postage prepaid, return receipt requested, to the person at the person's last
known address; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  By posting the notice of violation and order on the front door of the
living unit of the violator, if the person is not home.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D. 
Proof of service of the notice of violation and order must be made at the time
of service by a written declaration under penalty of perjury executed by the
person effecting service, declaring the time, date and manner in which service
was made.  (Ord. 19638 § 71, 2023:  <span style='color:black'>Ord. 18230 § 92,
2016:  </span>Ord. 16861 § 31, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 25, 2007:  Ord. 6370 § 9,
1983:  Ord. 1396 Art. III § 9, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.270 
Appeals.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  The office of the hearing examiner is designated to hear appeals by
parties aggrieved by actions of the manager under this title.  (Ord. 19638 § 72.
2023:  <span style='color:black'>Ord. 18230 § 93, 2016:  </span>Ord. 16861 §
32, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 26, 2007:  Ord. 1396 Art. III § 10, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.275 
Potentially dangerous animal - designation - requirements and responsibilities
of owner - registration - appeal - impoundment.</span></b> </p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
If the manager determines an animal's conduct falls within the definition of a
potentially dangerous animal, the manager shall designate the animal as
potentially dangerous.  Following such a designation the animal's owner shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Obtain a potentially dangerous animal registration, in addition to the
regular animal license, as set forth in section K.C.C. 11.04.035; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  The registration expires one year after issuance and the owner shall renew
the registration every twelve months.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
A registration will be issued to the owner of a potentially dangerous animal
only if, within twenty-four days of the designation, the owner transmits to the
manager two current, color, digital photographs in electronic format of the
animal, with a minimum size of three inches by five inches, and provides
sufficient proof of the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  An escape-proof fence, a proper enclosure, or other means of confinement
approved by the manager;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  A posted warning sign;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  The animal has been microchipped, with the microchip number provided to the
manager;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.  Current rabies vaccination;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
5.  Possession of a muzzle and a leash; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
6.  Possession of a current license tag and a brightly colored collar
sufficient to restrain the animal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
At all times the potentially dangerous animal must:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Wear its collar and license tag;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Be within an escape-proof fence, a proper enclosure, or within other means
of confinement approved by the manager when on the owner's premises; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  When off the owner's premises, be securely leashed, under the control of a
competent adult, and humanely muzzled or securely restrained in a carrier or
crate, made in accordance with International Air Transport Association
guidelines, while traveling in a vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D. 
This section does not apply to police dogs, as defined in RCW 4.24.410.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E. 
Animals found potentially dangerous by any jurisdiction of this or any other
state are subject to the same regulations as if designated potentially
dangerous by King County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F. 
Animals declared to be vicious under a prior version of this title shall
continue to comply with all conditions prescribed by the manager at the time
the animal was declared vicious.  Violation of any such condition shall
constitute a violation of the requirements for a potentially dangerous animal
and shall be subject to the same monetary penalty as a potentially dangerous
animal violation in K.C.C. 11.04.035.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G. 
During the entire appeal process of a potentially dangerous animal designation,
the owner shall keep the animal in a proper enclosure, or by other means
approved by the manager.  It is a violation of this chapter for the owner
appealing a declaration to allow or permit the animal to go beyond the premises
of the owner unless such animal is securely leashed, under the control of a
competent adult, and humanely muzzled or securely restrained in a carrier or
crate, made in accordance with International Air Transport Association
guidelines, while traveling in a vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H. 
The manager may immediately impound the animal upon a violation of any
provision of this section.  The animal's owner shall pay the costs of
confinement and the penalty imposed for the violation.  The manager shall
notify the owner of the reasons for impounding the animal, that the owner is
responsible for paying the costs of confinement, and that the animal will be
destroyed if the deficiencies for which the animal was confiscated are not
corrected within twenty-four days.  If within twenty-four days the owner cures
the deficiencies for which the animal was impounded to the satisfaction of the
manager, and the owner pays the costs of confinement and the penalty imposed,
then the owner may redeem the animal.  The manager shall destroy the impounded
animal if all violations of this section are not corrected, and all costs and
penalties are not paid, within twenty-four days of notification.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I. 
It is the duty of every animal owner to always keep the owner's animals under
proper supervision and control.  If an animal is designated potentially
dangerous, the duty is upon the animal owner to comply with this chapter.  When
an animal owner breaches these duties, the responsibility for any resulting
injury or damage shall be on the animal owner and not King County.  (Ord. 19638
§ 74, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.285 
Dangerous animal - designation - requirements and responsibilities of owner -
registration - inspection  - appeal - impoundment.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
If the manager determines an animal's conduct falls within the definition of a
dangerous animal, the manager shall designate the animal as dangerous. 
Following such a designation, the animal's owner shall:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Obtain a dangerous animal registration within twenty-four days of receiving
a dangerous animal designation, in addition to the regular animal license, as
set forth in section K.C.C. 11.04.035; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  The registration expires one year after issuance and the owner shall renew
the registration every twelve months.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
The manager shall issue a dangerous animal registration if, within twenty-four
days of the designation, the owner pays the fee prescribed in K.C.C. 11.04.035,
transmits to the manager two current, color, digital photographs in electronic
format of the animal, with a minimum size of three inches by five inches, and
provides sufficient proof of all the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  A proper enclosure and a posted warning sign;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  The animal has been microchipped, with the microchip number provided;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  Current rabies vaccination;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.  The animal has been spayed or neutered;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
5.  A muzzle and a leash;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
6.  A current license tag and a brightly colored collar sufficient to restrain
the animal; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
7.  A surety bond or liability insurance policy, such as a homeowner's or
renter's insurance policy, that:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                
a.  is issued by a surety insurer qualified under chapter 48.28 RCW or an
insurer qualified under Title 48 RCW;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                
b.  is in a form acceptable to the manager;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                
c.  provides at least five hundred thousand dollars coverage, with a reasonable
deductible;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                
d.  is payable to any person for any personal injuries inflicted by the
dangerous animal;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                
e.  shall be continuously maintained during the life of the registration;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                
f.  provides for prior written notification to the manager of cancellation or
material change; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>                
g.  a copy of such bond or liability policy is furnished to the manager, to
allow the manager a reasonable time to review and determine whether it is
sufficient to warrant a dangerous animal registration.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
The manager may inspect the premises where a dangerous animal is maintained at
any time.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D. 
At all times a dangerous animal must:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  Wear its collar and license tag;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  Be confined to a proper enclosure when on the owner's premises; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  When off the owner's premises, be securely leashed, under the control of a
competent adult, and humanely muzzled or securely restrained in a carrier or
crate, made in accordance with International Air Transport Association
guidelines, while traveling in a vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E. 
This section does not apply to police dogs as defined in RCW 4.24.410.  A
police dog is a dog used by a law enforcement agency specially trained for law
enforcement work and under the control of a dog handler.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F. 
The owner must notify the manager in writing in the event of a dangerous
animal's death, relocation or change in ownership.  For a change of ownership
or relocation, the registered owner shall provide the manager with:  written
notice, at least ten days in advance of any change, of the new owner's phone
number and complete street, mailing and email addresses; and proof that the new
owner and the new jurisdiction's animal control authority have been notified of
the animal's designation as dangerous.  If the change of ownership or
relocation is within King County, the owner shall satisfy all requirements of
this section before relocating the animal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G. 
An animal found dangerous by any jurisdiction of this state or any other state
is subject to the same requirements as if the animal was designated dangerous
by King County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H. 
A dangerous animal that is relocated outside King County is prohibited from
reentering the county without prior written consent of the manager and a valid
dangerous animal registration.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I. 
During the entire appeal process of a dangerous animal designation, the owner
shall keep the animal in a proper enclosure.  It is a violation of this chapter
for the owner appealing a declaration to allow or permit the animal to be
outside of the proper enclosure unless the animal is securely leashed, under
the control of a competent adult, and humanely muzzled or securely restrained
in an airline-approved carrier or crate while traveling in a vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            J. 
The manager shall immediately impound the animal upon a violation of this
section.  The animal's owner shall pay the costs of confinement and the penalty
imposed for the violation.  The manager shall notify the owner of the reasons
for impounding the animal, that the owner is responsible for paying the costs
of confinement, and that the animal will be destroyed if the deficiencies for
which the animal was confiscated are not corrected within twenty-four days.  If
within twenty-four days the owner cures the deficiencies for which the animal
was impounded to the satisfaction of the manager, and the owner pays the costs
of confinement and the penalty imposed, then the owner may redeem the animal. 
The manager shall destroy the impounded animal if all violations of this
section are not corrected, and all costs and penalties are not paid, within
twenty-four days of notification.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            K. 
It is the duty of every animal owner to always keep the animal under proper
supervision and control.  When an animal is declared dangerous, the duty is
upon the animal owner to comply with this chapter.  When an animal owner
breaches these duties, the responsibility for any resulting injury or damage
shall be on the animal owner and not King County.  (Ord. 19638 § 75, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.295 
Aggressive attacks causing human injury or death - impoundment - removal.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
The manager may immediately impound an animal when the animal aggressively
attacks and causes severe injury to or death of any human without provocation,
even where the animal had not previously been designated potentially dangerous
or dangerous.  If the animal is impounded, the manager shall designate the
animal as a dangerous animal and K.C.C. 11.04.285 shall apply, except the
animal shall remain impounded during the entire appeal process, if any.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
The manager may immediately impound an animal and the owner forfeits all rights
to the animal if the animal is not removed from the county in accordance with
an order of the manager under K.C.C. 11.04.222.  The animal's owner shall pay
the costs of confinement.  The manager shall notify the owner of the reason for
impounding the animal, that the owner is responsible for paying the costs of
confinement, and that the animal is the property of the manager.  If within
twenty-four days the owner provides to the manager a location for the animal to
live outside of the county, including the name, address, phone number, and
email address of the person or organization taking ownership of the animal to
the satisfaction of the manager, and the owner pays the costs of confinement
and the penalty imposed, then the owner may redeem the animal.  The owner shall
ensure the animal is removed from the county immediately upon redemption.  The
manager shall make a disposition of the animal consistent with the options in K.C.C.
11.04.210.E.1. through E.5. if, within twenty-four days of notification, the
owner has not paid the costs of confinement and provided the information
required by this section.  (Ord. 19638 § 76, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.300 
Civil penalty and abatement costs &#8209; liability of owner.</span></b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The civil penalty
and the cost of abatement are also personal obligations of the animal owner. 
The prosecuting attorney on behalf of King County may collect the civil penalty
and the abatement work costs by use of all appropriate legal remedies.  (Ord.
1396 Art. III § 13, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.310 
Costs of enforcement action.</b>  In addition to costs and disbursements
provided for by statute, the prevailing party in a collection action under this
chapter may, in the court's discretion, be allowed interest and a reasonable
attorney's fee.  The prosecuting attorney shall seek such costs, interest, and
reasonable attorney's fees on behalf of King County when the county is the
prevailing party.  (Ord. 1396 Art. III § 14, 1971).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.330 
Additional rules and regulations.</b>  The regional animal services section is
authorized to make and enforce rules and regulations, not inconsistent with the
provisions of this chapter section, and it is unlawful to violate or fail to
comply with any of such rules and regulations.  All of such rules and
regulations shall be reduced to writing and adopted in accordance with K.C.C.
chapter 2.98.  (Ord. 16861 § 34, 2010:  Ord. 6370 § 12, 1983).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.335 
Waiver, refund, or amnesty periods for penalties and fees.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
The manager section may, in full or in part, waive, refund or provide amnesty
periods for outstanding civil penalties, licensing fees, late licensing penalty
fees, adoption fees, and redemption and sheltering fees, in whole or in part,
when doing so would further the goals of this title and be in the public
interest.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
In determining whether a waiver should apply, the manager shall consider the
following elements:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
1.  The reason the animal was impounded;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
2.  The violation's reason or the basis, nature, duration, and likelihood of
recurrence;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
3.  The total amount of the fees charged as compared with the gravity of the
violation; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>             
4.  The effect on the owner, the animal's welfare and the regional animal
services section if the fee or penalties are not waived.  (Ord. 19638 § 77, 2023: 
Ord. 16861 § 35, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 29, 2007:  Ord. 10809 § 7, 1993: Ord. 7986
§ 3, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.350 
Misdemeanors.</b>  It is a misdemeanor to:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
Intentionally cause, aid, or abet any violation of K.C.C.11.04.230 or
11.04.250, by any act or omission;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
Fail to comply with a manager's order related to an animal designated as
potentially dangerous, vicious, or dangerous after the animal has committed two
violations of this chapter;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
Fail to comply with a manager's order related to an animal designated as
dangerous;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D. 
Cause an animal to injure a human or domesticated animal acting in a lawful
manner;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            E. 
Own or maintain a pet shop, hobby kennel or hobby cattery, pet daycare
facility, animal shelter, or pet grooming service without the operating permit
or permits required by K.C.C. chapter 11.04, after having committed a related
violation;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            F. 
Sell, adopt, transfer ownership, or trade an unlicensed pet, except in
accordance with K.C.C. 11.04.030, after committing a related violation;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            G. 
Sell, adopt, transfer ownership, or trade an animal knowing it to be ill or
injured, without disclosing the animal's illness or injury;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            H. 
Remove any animal from the possession of the animal care and control authority
without permission of the manager or without paying all lawful charges;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            I. 
Obstruct any animal care and control officer in the performance of any official
duty;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            J. 
Within a two-year period, receive five or more notices of violations or
infractions issued under this title; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            K. 
Permit livestock to run at large in a stock restricted area.</span>  <span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord. 19638 § 79,
2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.360 
Gross misdemeanors.</b></span>  <span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>It is a gross misdemeanor for anyone to keep, maintain,
control, or retain custody of any animal in conjunction with or for the
purpose, whether in whole or in part, of aiding, abetting, or conducting any
illegal activity or committing any crime.</span>  <span style='font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord. 19638 § 80, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal align=center style='text-align:center'><b>IV.  MANDATORY SPAY
AND NEUTER PROGRAM</b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.400 
Mandatory alteration - exceptions.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
A person may not harbor, keep, or maintain any nonjuvenile pet that has not
been altered, unless the person holds an unaltered pet license for the animal.</span></p>

<p class=MsoBodyText style='margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            B.  Guide dogs in training
and police service dogs are exempted from this section.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
Any nonjuvenile pet adopted from an animal shelter in King County must be
altered before transfer to the owner.  (Ord. 19638 § 81. 2023:  Ord. 10423 § 2,
1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.410 
Voucher for alteration.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  When issuing a license for an unaltered pet, the manager
may provide to the applicant a voucher for paying all or part of the cost of an
altering operation by a licensed veterinarian, with the amount of the voucher
established by the manager based upon available resources and upon the council
providing appropriation authority.  The manager shall compile, maintain, and
make available to the public a list of veterinarians who accept the vouchers as
full or partial payment for altering.  Vouchers are redeemable through the King
County treasury by veterinarians who have performed an alteration on a pet
licensed in King County as an unaltered pet.  (Ord. 19638 § 82. 2023:  Ord.
16861 § 36, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 30, 2007:  Ord. 10423 § 24, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=Normal align=center style='text-align:center'><b>V.  OTHER PROVISIONS</b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.500 
Euthanasia rate targets.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A. 
It is the policy of King County that a maximum euthanasia rate target is set to
measure the progress towards reducing the rates of pets euthanized by the regional
animal services section or its designees.  The euthanasia rates must calculated
based on the total number of live pets taken into King County custody to
include stray, homeless, abandoned, unwanted or surrendered animals, and
animals euthanized at an owner's request.  The euthanasia rates must exclude
animals euthanized at the order of the director and those animals not in the
custody of King County but brought to a King County shelter by their owner or
guardian for the purposes of licensing, or clinic services, such as alterations
and vaccinations, should the manager make those services available to the
public.  The calculation of the euthanasia rate for a given year should include
the inventory of pets carried over from the preceding year and exclude the
inventory of pets carried over to the subsequent year.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B. 
The total number of pets euthanized by the regional animal services section is
not to exceed fifteen percent.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C. 
The manager should, to the extent feasible, calculate other measures of
euthanasia rates or live release rates that enable comparison with other
agencies.  (Ord. 19638 § 83. 2023:  Ord. 16861 § 37, 2010:  Ord. 15801 § 31,
2007:  Ord. 10423 § 6, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.510 
Unaltered dogs and cats - advertising requirements.</span></b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  No person in
unincorporated King County shall publish or advertise to King County residents
the availability of any unaltered cat or dog unless the publication or
advertisement includes: the unaltered animal's license number or the animal's
juvenile license number, provided, however that nothing in this chapter shall
prohibit licensed breeders from advertising in national publications for sale
of a planned litter or litters.  (Ord. 10423 § 9, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>11.04.530 
Exemptions from chapter.</b>  This chapter does not apply to dogs and cats in
the custody of a research facility registered or licensed by the United States
Department of Agriculture and regulated by 7 United States Code 2131, et seq. 
(Ord. 19638 § 85. 2023:  Ord. 10423 § 20, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.580 
Canvassing for compliance program.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The manager may develop and implement a twelve-month
program to canvass for compliance with the licensing requirements of this title. 
The program must be directed at households within unincorporated areas of King
County and cities under contract with King County for animal care control
services.  Regional animal services section employees and persons or
organizations under contract to the regional animal service section performing
the canvassing may issue pet licenses and collect license fees.  The manager
shall annually review the canvassing program.  Funding must be reviewed
annually based upon an evaluation of the efficacy of the canvassing program.  (Ord.
19638 § 88. 2023:  Ord. 15801 § 36, 2007:  Ord. 10423 § 27, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            11.04.595 
Severability.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  If any provision of this title or its application to any person or
circumstance is held invalid, the remainder of the title or the application of
the provision to other persons or circumstances is not affected.  (Ord. 19638 §
89, 2023).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;text-align:justify;line-height:
normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

</div>

</body>

</html>
